<section class="case-study reveal">
  <div class="case-left">
    <div class="case-tag">Case Study &mdash; In Practice</div>
    <div style="margin-top: auto;">
      <div class="case-novel-title">The House on Mango Street</div>
      <div class="case-novel-author">Sandra Cisneros</div>
      <p class="case-novel-system">Social isolation and identity formation. A young person&rsquo;s sense of possibility shrinks when their world is small by design.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="case-right">
    <p><strong>The novel:</strong> Students read Sandra Cisneros&rsquo;s <em>House on Mango Street</em> through Literary Science, analyzing the consequences of social isolation on identity formation. The novel renders a system: what happens when possibility is shaped not by ability but by proximity.</p>
    <p><strong>The overlay:</strong> Literary analysis became the basis for research on their peers&rsquo; career aspirations versus representation. They discovered that a high percentage of their peers wanted to become healthcare professionals&mdash;but did not personally know a single healthcare professional. The asset existed (desire). The flow was blocked (no connection to the profession).</p>
    <p><strong>The hypothesis:</strong> The system Cisneros rendered&mdash;isolation shaping aspiration&mdash;was operating in their own community. Strategic Response identified the gap: create the connection that the system had never provided.</p>
    <div class="case-homage">
      <div class="case-homage-label">The Homage</div>
      <p>Using their literacy skills&mdash;proposal writing, data storytelling, strategic communication&mdash;students designed The Net Gala: a networking event modeled after the Met Gala that brought together 100 young people with 50 healthcare professionals. The Net Gala is now NewComm&rsquo;s official annual fundraiser.</p>
      <p>A novel became an event. An event became an institution. It is Sandra Cisneros&rsquo;s ideas given legs.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="homage-strip">
  <p>Every NewComm project is, at its heart, an homage to an author. The project is how students honor the intellectual tradition they&rsquo;ve inherited&mdash;by doing something with it.</p>
  <span class="h-attr">Projects as Homage</span>
</div>

